                <pb facs="0074" n="36" sameAs="frus:frus1951v03p1/pg36"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>The Council Deputies, in their meeting of January 22, discussed further the
                    future composition of the NAC and, with the
                    exception of the United States representative present, agreed upon a draft
                    statement that would substitute for certain parts of the Council’s original
                    terms of reference, D–1/1, and the Wilgress draft introduced at the meeting on the 17th. Ambassador
                        Gifford, quoting the draft and
                    reporting the meeting in telegram Depto 445,
                    January 23, not printed, said that at the close of the discussion the Deputies
                    expressed the hope that the United States would soon remove the last hurdle on
                    reorganization of the top NATO structure by
                    making its position known. (740.5/1–2351)</p>
            </div>
